TRUCT_0005>\nIf <MATH_0005> is locally Noetherian, then\n<STRUCT_0006>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(3)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008> are of finite type over <MATH_0009> and\n<MATH_0010> is finite over <MATH_0011>, then <MATH_0012> is of finite type over\n<MATH_0013><FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>If <MATH_0014> maps into an affine open of <MATH_0015>\nthis follows from\nMore on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThe general case follows using\nMore on Algebra, Lemma <REF_0005>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>, and\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(4)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0016> satisfies (RS*), then <MATH_0017> satisfies (RS)\nbecause (RS) covers exactly those cases of (RS*) where\n<MATH_0018>, <MATH_0019>, <MATH_0020> are Artinian local.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0dc643a05b0a04a167f439a9699b453a21fc7f8600a99e6df4f6d152685b15a1", "unit_id": "tag:0CXN:prose-0002"}
